module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionFullyFaithful.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.CompletionFunctor.FullyFaithful
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.FormalSections

/-!
# Completion on vector bundles is fully faithful exactly when formal functions hold

Let `I ⊆ 𝔞` be ideals of a Noetherian ring `A` and let `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)`. Stacks 0EKQ asserts
that the completion functor `Coh(𝒪_U) ⟶ Coh(U, I𝒪_U)` of Stacks 0880 is fully faithful on the
full subcategory of finite locally free objects, provided

1. `A` is `I`-adically complete and has a dualizing complex;
2. for every associated prime `𝔭` of `A` with `𝔭 ∉ V(I)` and `V(𝔭) ∩ V(I) ⊄ V(𝔞)`, and every
   `𝔮 ∈ V(𝔭) ∩ V(𝔞)`, one has `dim((A/𝔭)_𝔮) > cd(A, I) + 1`;
3. for every prime `𝔭` with `𝔭 ∉ V(I)` and `V(𝔭) ∩ V(I) ⊆ V(𝔞)`, one has `depth(A_𝔭) ≥ 2`.

This file reduces that conclusion, with no hypothesis at all, to the theorem on formal functions
in degree zero for the internal homs: full faithfulness on the finite locally free objects holds
exactly when `Γ(U, SheafHom(ℱ, 𝒢)) ⟶ lim_n Γ(U, SheafHom(ℱ, 𝒢) / Iⁿ SheafHom(ℱ, 𝒢))` is an
isomorphism for all finite locally free coherent `ℱ`, `𝒢`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.bijective_completionFunctor_map_iff_isIso_globalSectionsToLimit` — on a
  locally Noetherian scheme with a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf, the completion functor is bijective
  on the morphisms `G ⟶ F` if and only if `Stacks.Algebraization.globalSectionsToLimit` is an
  isomorphism for `SheafHom(G, F)`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.completionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree_iff` — the same equivalence
  quantified over the finite locally free objects, at `U = Spec(A) ∖ V(𝔞)` and `I𝒪_U`.

## Implementation notes

### What is reduced, and what is left open

Neither of the conditions (1)–(3) is consumed: the equivalence is an identity of the completion
functor, true on any locally Noetherian scheme and any quasi-coherent ideal sheaf. So no clause
of 0EKQ is proved, and the attribute records the reduction. The right-hand side is Stacks 0EIG at
the coherent module `SheafHom(ℱ, 𝒢)`, which is where the source's hypotheses (1)–(3) are
consumed, and it is not assumed here — it is one side of an equivalence.

Stacks 0EIG itself is in the library, as
`Stacks.Algebraization.FormalSectionsII.isIso_globalToFormalSections`, under the tag's own
conditions (1)–(3) together with the three hypotheses that the library's Stacks 0EG2,
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_comparisonMap`, carries. Its conclusion is stated for the arrow
`Stacks.Algebraization.FormalSectionsII.globalToFormalSections`, the comparison of Stacks 0EG2
read on the largest neighbourhood of the formal locus, and not for
`Stacks.Algebraization.globalSectionsToLimit`; the two arrows are not identified anywhere, so the
right-hand side of the equivalence below is not obtained from it as it stands.

The direction that produces full faithfulness is Stacks 0883 at the level of a single hom-set,
`Stacks.Algebraization.completionFunctor_map_bijective`, and so goes through the comparison of
Stacks 0882 rather than through Stacks 0EKP: the chain (2) ⇒ (3) ⇒ (4) of Stacks 0EKP, whose
state is described in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/CompletionFullyFaithful/Basic.lean`, is not needed
for 0EKQ. The converse direction is the one Stacks 0EKP states as (4) ⇒ (3) and leaves to the
reader: the chain of bijections of Stacks 0883 is read backwards, which is possible because every
link but the comparison with the limit is a bijection on the nose.

### Shape of the two sides

The ideal sheaf `I𝒪_U` is `Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafNearVanishing`, the quasi-coherent
ideal sheaf generated by the image of `I` in `Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`, which is the spelling
`Stacks.Algebraization.formalSections` uses for the same object. Full faithfulness on the finite
locally free objects is `Stacks.Algebraization.CompletionFullyFaithfulOnFiniteLocallyFree`,
bijectivity of the completion map on each hom set, and the formal-functions comparison is
`Stacks.Algebraization.globalSectionsToLimit`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EIG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EIG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKP)
